## 2) Language & Trust Rules (Non-Negotiable)

### Confidence-aware phrasing ladder
- High confidence: “Best next move… likely… expect noticeable…”
- Medium confidence: “Most likely… try… typically…”
- Low confidence: “Directional guidance… worth testing… if/then…”

### Null vs Peak truthfulness
- Nulls are cancellations. Do not claim that treatments “fill” severe nulls.
- Peaks are more treatment-responsive (esp. ringing/decay).

### Integration-sensitive band
- Any problem in 80–120 Hz must carry “integration-sensitive” caution and softened phrasing.

Never use absolute certainty (“this will fix it completely”).

---

## 3) Defaults (Locked)

- Default mode: two-channel sweet spot
- Band: 20–120 Hz
- Top Problems: 3
- Seed room if blank: ~12×16×8 ft
- Default seat placement: centered, ~38% of room length from front wall
- Opening default: off; when added default type `doorway`, ~3 ft, door closed
- Default mains: arranged into reasonable triangle; lowest strong bass default ~55–60 Hz
- Default sub:
  - position: front wall at ~1/4 room width from left (clearance respected)
  - default mode: sealed
  - sealed lowest strong bass default: ~28–30 Hz
  - preset default: Balanced
- Default treatments: none
- Default tuned trap target: dominant peak region center
- Default seatLocked: false
- Default allowNearfieldSuggestions: false

Avoid perfect symmetry defaults.

---

## 4) Prohibited Features (v1 MUST NOT)

- Multi-sub simulation
- Multiple openings
- Non-rectangular rooms
- Couch/listening-area averaging (multi-seat)
- Detailed crossover/phase/time alignment modeling
- Changing Top Problems from 3
- Removing treatment caps or diminishing returns
- Overconfident phrasing or claiming exact dB accuracy

---

## 5) Implementation Guidance (How to Work)

### Build in phases as defined in `/docs/planning/README.md`
Follow the build order phases. Do not skip ahead with scope creep.

### When uncertain
- Prefer the simplest interpretation consistent with the planning docs.
- Add TODO notes instead of inventing new features.
- If a needed decision is missing, do not guess. Add a note to update planning docs first.

### Outputs must be stable
- Use region-based logic (not single Hz bins).
- Use hysteresis for severity to prevent jitter during dragging.

---

## 6) Acceptance Criteria (Quick)
A change is acceptable only if:
- It does not violate any hard rule above.
- Top Problems remains exactly 3.
- Recommendations remain exactly 3 actions.
- Problems remain small regions.
- Sealed + ported modes both work, with port/driver split near Fb.
- Treatments snap, have caps, and show diminishing returns UI.
- A/B snapshots work exactly as defined.

End of rules.
